  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-ReCIPE Civic Space and Digital Rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ReCIPE project in Cambodia aims to cultivate a rights-respecting digital ecosystem that is values-based, human-centric and safe forcivil society actors and human rights defenders. To achieve this goal, the project has focused on 3 specific objectives (i) to increase collaboration between national and regional levels to create vibrant and safe online civic spaces, (ii) to improve digital rights mechanisms and policies that make governments and corporate actors accountable, and (iii) to foster equitable access to safe and secure online social and political activities.

Oxfam in Cambodia (OiC) is one of the successful countries that was selected to be co-applicant organizations from the 10 focus countries of the Global North and the Global South. The co-applicant CSOs demonstrate higher levels of digital literacy and have better access to resources for engaging in the digital arena than other CSOs, but they are not immune to the overall constraints and threats facing CSOs, specifically cyber-attacks, data protection and online harassment.

In Cambodia, CCC is one of the implementing partners is working with national networks and think tanks focusing on digital advocacy and policy issues that engage government ministries, academia, private sector and civil society. In sub-national level, CCC will facilitate provincial NGOs and CBOs in 16 provinces through the existing platform of Provincial NGOs meeting.</narrative>
  </description>
